# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Path-level only.
#
# The www → apex redirect canNOT live here: Pages matches `_redirects` sources
# against the path alone and ignores any scheme/hostname, so a rule like
# `https://www.example.org/* https://example.org/:splat 301` silently does
# nothing (tested — www returned 200 and served the site). It is configured as a
# Cloudflare Redirect Rule on the zone instead; see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.

# The News & Events pages were removed. Anything that linked to them lands on the
# homepage rather than a 404. Safe to delete once nothing references them.
/news      /  301
/news/*    /  301
/events    /  301
/events/*  /  301

# Short link to share the Blog section. Exact matches only — /blog/<slug>/ is
# where internal posts live, so there must be no /blog/* splat here.
/blog      /research/#blog  301
/blog/     /research/#blog  301
